From 9d12c0cfbffdda1def0c9c9d61b627c4701768a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:20:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Dispersed first-home placement as a season switch
 (placement 1)

Adds `placement` (0 = wedge, 1 = dispersed small groups) and an unused
`r_max_ceiling` to the conquest block (offsets 77 and 78, reserve now 80).
placement 0 keeps every rule as before.

- permutation-rules: `geometry::home_nation` / `is_home_heartland`. Under
  placement 1 each heartland ring r is walked in index order and province
  i goes to nation (i + o_r) mod 6, o_r from sha256(domain, genesis seed,
  r): every nation takes r provinces per ring, six positions apart, in r
  different wedges; neighbours differ; the same seed gives the same map.
- program: PlaceHome checks `home_nation` instead of the wedge; OpenProvince
  gives a heartland keep (and its heartland safety) to `home_nation`;
  DeclareSiege's heartland refusal follows `is_home_heartland` under
  placement 1. FileTicket (legacy M1) stays wedge-based.
- off-chain mirrors: web home candidates (`fgeo.homeNation`,
  `home.seasonPlace`), bots `home_sites`, verifier v11 PlaceHome check.
- tests: geometry unit tests incl. a vector pinned against the JS mirror,
  LiteSVM `tests/placement.rs` and a dispersed heartland siege case in
  `tests/conquest.rs`, node `web-frontier-placement.test.mjs`; ABI vectors
  and the generated web SDK regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2bji8di3758qGdC2v1
